  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of IDPs and Returnees in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan is facing an unprecedented humanitarian crisis with a very real risk of systemic collapse and human catastrophe. The objective of this project is to ensure the continuity of services for vulnerable returnees and internally displaced persons (IDPs) and address their immediate needs in terms of non-food items (NFI) and shelter needs in key targeted provinces while integrating protection principles throughout the response. To achieve this, under this project IOM is addressing the humanitarian needs of vulnerable undocumented Afghan migrants returning from the Islamic Republic of Iran and Pakistan and IDPs in the locations of return or high return areas through cash for winterization complemented with in-kind, winter clothing and blankets.</narrative>
  </description>
